Z||000000||Monkeyman||07-01-2001||08:55 AM||||The door buttons on my locks are backwards.  When I press 'Lock', the doors unlock and vice versa.  I've double checked all the wiring, etc and it seems to be fine.  What can I do to fix this?  I'd like to add RKE, but don't want to mess things up or get things backwards.  What else can I check?<P>TIA<P>MM||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||07-01-2001||10:48 AM||||Double check your wires at the junction block above the fuse box. Reverse the wires if possible.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-01-2001||11:55 AM||||I'll check that.  Thanx, Keith.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||07-02-2001||10:17 AM||||I believe there is a Right side and a Left side switch.  Could you have them on the worng sides?||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierobaby||07-02-2001||03:15 PM||||hes right there is a left and right side switch...I just ordered a right side (drivers side) switch because my poor little lock unlock things rubbed off...its possble you have them switched..if you don't just switch them and have lock on the side closest to the steering wheel<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-02-2001||04:51 PM||||I bought the p/lock assy in its' entirety.  Wiring harness, actuators, switches and switch housings all together.  The switches were still in the housings (the part that actually attaches to the doors).  It would be unlikely (but possible, I guess) that the switches are on the wrong sides.  I need to remove the dash (again <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">) to check the wiring to the windshield washer and run the speaker wiring to the doors (stupid me forgot to do these while I had the dash out the 1st time).  I'll look at the wiring at the junction box as Indiana_resto_guy suggested and go from there.<P>Thanx. <P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
